  "shipping_reason": "Hard floor, with one constant per calendar month. Passes every check the shipping rule names, as first written: C0, C1 (0.077), C1b, C2 (-0.094) and C3 (0.117 against 0.15); also C3r, C3x (2020 to 2021: 0.124) and C4. The detection curve passes C3 (0.072) but fails the 2016 placebo C2 (-0.114 against 0.10), so the rule moves to the hard floor. Until 15 Nov the detection curve with one year-round constant shipped under the revised check C3r; it failed C3 (0.207) because its error followed the season.",
  "unit": "Aqua-equivalent fire cells",
  "unit_note": "One fire cell is a 1 km square (0.01 degree) with fire in one satellite pass. Before February 2012: what Aqua MODIS reported. From February 2012: what Aqua would have reported, computed from VIIRS with the hard floor (only fire cells at or above a measured strength cut-off are counted), scaled by a constant fitted for each calendar month because the two sensors' relation follows the season.",
